 - [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When two or more accepted submissions derive from the same starting visit state, the system SHALL preserve every original submission of that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission names no base revision, the system SHALL create the visit and store the payload as its initial revision.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission's base revision ID is the visit's current head revision, the system SHALL append the payload as the new head revision.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a submission's base revision ID is not the visit's current head revision, the system SHALL store the payload as a competing revision, leave the head revision unchanged, and mark the visit as having unresolved review work.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: The system SHALL not alter a stored revision's payload, author ID, or server receipt time after acceptance.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a caller retrieves current state for a visit with unresolved review work, the system SHALL return the head revision, the unresolved status, and the visit's unresolved competing revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a coordinator resolution names a competing revision as the outcome, the system SHALL set that revision as the head, retain the losing revisions, and mark the visit as resolved.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: While a visit has unresolved review work, the system SHALL retain the unresolved status until a coordinator resolution changes it.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: The system SHALL not combine, reorder, or partially apply the payloads of competing revisions.
